{"adjudications":[{"id":"F1","decision":"confirmed","reason":"In the revision, Julius's 'No' now answers 'Do you mean to kill me?' directly. That reads as a flat promise not to shoot, which conflicts with the later 'He raised the revolver.' In the source, Julius makes the threat conditional ('Not if you keep your voice down') and answers Kramenin's money question. Restoring two short source lines fixes this.","evidence":[{"document":"025.revision","paragraph":18,"quote":"“Do you mean to kill me?”"},{"document":"025.revision","paragraph":19,"quote":"“No. I want Jane Finn.”"},{"document":"025.source","paragraph":31,"quote":"“Not if you keep your voice down."},{"document":"025.source","paragraph":35,"quote":"“What do you want? Money?”"}]},{"id":"F2","decision":"rejected","reason":"The threat can be read from what remains. The reader has just seen the automatic and the countdown. Kramenin's nerve fails as they pass the hotel servants, and Julius rides with 'his hand in his coat pocket', so the mechanism is still implied. The plan does not list this as essential, so cutting it is a legitimate tradeoff.","evidence":[{"document":"025.revision","paragraph":49,"quote":"A cry hovered on the Russian’s lips, but at the last minute his nerve failed him."},{"document":"025.revision","paragraph":52,"quote":"Julius, his hand in his coat pocket, was urbane to the last degree"}]},{"id":"F3","decision":"rejected","reason":"Julius's opposition is still clear in the revision: he demands 'What the devil are you driving at?', cries 'Darn you!' and orders 'Jane, you stay where you are.' Jane's line in 026 is consistent with this. The motive stays unexplained and Julius stays ambiguous, so the cut is an acceptable compression.","evidence":[{"document":"025.revision","paragraph":98,"quote":"“What the devil are you driving at?” demanded Julius."},{"document":"025.revision","paragraph":102,"quote":"“Darn you!” cried Julius. “Jane, you stay where you are.”"}]}],"replacements":[{"old":"“No. I want Jane Finn.”","new":"“Not if you keep your voice down.”

“What do you want? Money?”

“No. I want Jane Finn.”","reason":"Restores from the source the conditional menace and Kramenin's money-minded question.","finding_ids":["F1"]},{"old":"“Then you won’t do as I ask you?”","new":"","reason":"Optional cut. This exchange repeats the earlier 'You ask an impossibility' and offsets the restored lines.","finding_ids":[]},{"old":"“You ask an impossibility.”","new":"","reason":"Second half of the redundant repeated exchange.","finding_ids":[]},{"old":"studying him attentively with","new":"studying him with","reason":"Minimal trim to meet the word target.","finding_ids":[]},{"old":"Presently the telephone","new":"The telephone","reason":"Minimal trim to meet the word target.","finding_ids":[]}],"remaining_concerns":["Removing paragraphs 30–31 may leave empty paragraph slots. Paragraph 29's 'man to fear' now leads directly into 'Sure that’s a pity for you', which still reads naturally."]}
